{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>He too shall be blessed.</b> Above all, and he said thus to teach that one who is blessed on earth by the mouth of the fathers is as one blessed by the mouth of the Elohei Amen (Isaiah 65:16)." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> 'And Isaac trembled with a great trembling' — Isaac trembled two tremblings: one upon the altar, and one here. And Scripture says 'exceedingly' to say that this trembling was greater than that trembling which he trembled upon the altar." "<b>And in Bereshit Rabbah.</b> Is it possible for a man who has two sons, one entering and one leaving, and he trembles? That would be astonishing! Rather, at the hour Esau entered, Gehinnom entered with him. R. Natan in the name of R. Acha: the walls of the house began to shake. That is what is said: <b>Who then?</b> — who is he that is destined to roast here, I and my sons? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Not you and not your son, but rather he — <b>the one who hunted game</b> — he went to hunt and was hunted. End of quotation."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:34.248421074Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}